<title>FRANCE: Air France increases cargo tonnage share at ADP.</title>
<headline>Air France increases cargo tonnage share at ADP.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air France increased its share of global air cargo tonnage handled at the two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in the first eleven months of 1996, Aeroport de Paris (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Air France's took a 55.6 percent share of the ADP Jan-Nov cargo tonnage of 1,013,379 tonnes compared to 53.8 percent a year earlier.</p>
<p>Federal Express was in second place increasing its share to 6.8 percent in Jan-Nov 1996 from 5.9 percent in 1995 as a whole.</p>
<p>The top 10 cargo-handling airlines at ADP, by tonnage share, in the first eleven months of 1996, against total 1995 share, were:</p>
<p>			    Jan-Oct 1996	    1995</p>
<p>Air France		   55.6		   53.8</p>
<p>FedEx			   6.8		    5.9</p>
<p>Air France Europe	   3.9		    4.4</p>
<p>American Airlines	   2.0		    1.9</p>
<p>L'Aeropostale		 1.9		    1.8</p>
<p>Cathay Pacific		1.9		    1.8</p>
<p>Air Canada		    1.7		    2.0</p>
<p>Japan Airlines		1.6		    1.6</p>
<p>Air Jet			 1.3		    n.a.</p>
<p>United Airlines	     1.3		    1.4</p>
<p>-- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
